2026-11-22T11:31:36.7485502Z [1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer[0m
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7552518Z [32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7559016Z [0m
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7559482Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7560134Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7560319Z 
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7560455Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7560760Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7560936Z 
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7561063Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7561339Z    if you are ready to continue.
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7561465Z 
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7561741Z 3. Create the system users [34m(uids [30001..30008])[0m and groups [34m(gid 30000)[0m
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7562081Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7562370Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7562614Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7562722Z 
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7562838Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7563009Z 
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7563146Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7563405Z    can use Nix.
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7563498Z 
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7563564Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7563676Z 
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7566341Z [32m[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7566790Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7571631Z 
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7571809Z I will:
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7571934Z 
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7572128Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7572525Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7572936Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7573324Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7573600Z  - install Nix in /nix
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7573857Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7574667Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7575042Z    /root
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7585079Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7585426Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7592371Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7592988Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7593210Z 
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7593453Z [32m[4;32mReady to continue?
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7593743Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7606257Z 
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7606746Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7613743Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7614165Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7614872Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7615004Z 
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7615144Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7615330Z 
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7615490Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7615823Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7616001Z 
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7616081Z If you would like to
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7616301Z see the output, try like this:
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7616450Z 
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7616615Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-11-22T11:31:36.7616900Z   $ sh ./install-nix
